// voxel_probe — Phase B fixture for the voxel-engine integration plan
// (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-09-voxel-engine-integration.md`).
//
// Drives the GPU `apply_ability` dispatcher with two self-cast
// world-primitive verbs:
//
//   1. PlaceTestVoxel (apply_ability 1) — fires once at tick=0.
//      Dispatcher writes one EffectPlaceVoxelApplied record (kind=60)
//      with `slot[2]=caster_slot`, `slot[3]=kind_hash("test_voxel")`.
//
//   2. HarvestTestVoxel (apply_ability 2) — fires on tick % 10 == 5
//      (so first at tick=5, then 15, 25, ...). Dispatcher writes one
//      EffectHarvestApplied record (kind=59) with `slot[2]=caster_slot`,
//      `slot[3]=kind_hash`, `slot[4]=amount=1`.
//
// **Sequential-by-tick design (P5 determinism).** Each tick at most ONE
// of the two verbs is eligible — Place fires only at tick==0, Harvest
// only on the % 10 == 5 cadence. This avoids any chronicle-ring
// contention and gives the behavioral pins clean tick-window contracts:
//
//   * tick 0  → Place fires
//   * tick 5  → Harvest fires (clears the placed voxel)
//   * tick 10 → no verb fires
//   * tick 15 → Harvest fires again (no-op, cell already clear)
//   * ...
//
// **One-agent design.** Slot 0 is the lone caster (creature_type=1,
// "worker"). The runtime constructs the agent at world origin
// (0.0, 0.0, 0.0); both verbs are self-cast so the dispatcher's
// `caster_slot` matches `target_slot`, both = 0.
//
// **No CPU oracle here.** Phase D will diff CPU↔GPU once the .sim
// gains a non-trivial verb chain. Phase B is a GPU-only producer +
// host-side voxel-grid drain pin.
//
// AbilityRegistry slot order (alphabetised by file name, matches
// `voxel_probe_runtime::voxel_probe_constants`):
//   HarvestTestVoxel.ability → AbilityId 1
//   PlaceTestVoxel.ability   → AbilityId 2
//
// The runtime pins these via `binding_check`-shape constants so a
// drift in `build_registry`'s ordering surfaces as a panic at fixture
// construction.

event Tick { }

entity Worker : Agent { }

// NOTE: no top-level `scoring { ... }` block. A `scoring { Name = K }`
// entry adds a mask-less utility row to the scoring kernel — useful
// when an action has constant utility and no mask gate, but for
// mask-gated verbs it forces the argmax to ALWAYS pick that constant-
// utility action even when the mask doesn't pass. Each verb supplies
// its score via the `score K` clause in the verb body, gated by the
// emitted mask row, which is the right shape for tick-windowed verbs
// like the two below.

// PlaceTestVoxel — fires at tick=0 only. Self-cast. AbilityId 2 (the
// alphabetised registry slot for `PlaceTestVoxel.ability`).
verb PlaceTestVoxel(self) =
  action PlaceTestVoxelAction
  when (self.alive && world.tick == 0)
  apply_ability 2 by self target self
  score 1.0

// HarvestTestVoxel — fires on tick % 10 == 5. Self-cast. AbilityId 1
// (the alphabetised registry slot for `HarvestTestVoxel.ability`).
verb HarvestTestVoxel(self) =
  action HarvestTestVoxelAction
  when (self.alive && world.tick > 0 && (world.tick % 10 == 5))
  apply_ability 1 by self target self
  score 1.0
